  "name": "InfiniteMap",
  "previewIconUrl": "",
  "shortDescription": "Endless scrolling map that recycles chunks around the player.",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Creates an endless map (Vampire Survivors style) by recycling a 3x3 grid of chunk instances around the player. Place 9 instances of your chunk object in a 3x3 grid, then call \"Update infinite map\" every frame with the exact pixel size of one chunk. Chunks that leave the view on one side reappear on the opposite side, so the player never reaches the edge. Use \"Center object on player\" to keep backgrounds or overlays following the player across the endless map. Each chunk must be at least as large as the game view (screen width and height), otherwise gaps may appear at the edges of the map.",
  "tags": [
    "infinite",
    "map",
    "endless",
    "chunks",
    "scrolling",
    "top-down",
    "survivors"
  ],
